Your system prompt holds this lane's context pack, which is also at .ropeshift/context/pack.md. It is where you start and not a limit: the context_get, decision_search, requirement_get, and question_search tools read the rest of what this workspace holds.

Commit only the files you created or edited in this lane, by naming each one: never stage the whole worktree with git add -A, git add ., or git commit -a. Leave any other changed or untracked file as it is, such as a cache your tools or your agent's setup wrote: ropeshift reports each one when the lane ends, and the orchestrator decides whether it belongs to the project or to the repository's .gitignore.

When the work is done, or cannot go on, call the lane_report tool once with its outcome, then end your turn.

Never wait for CI, a review, or a merge: after you push, ropeshift reads the checks and starts the review and the merge, so call lane_report and end your turn. Do not sleep, poll, or watch for them, and do not read their status: a command that does is denied.
